WEBVTT

00:04.690 --> 00:08.040
Why am I joining Inukami-senpai's training?

00:08.320 --> 00:11.990
Commander Siglis and the knights 
accompanied Kazuki, didn't they?

00:12.480 --> 00:15.600
We received the same request
for Hero Kazuki's training,

00:15.600 --> 00:18.900
but I refused since you had just 
come back from the forest.

00:18.900 --> 00:22.310
However, His Majesty 
petitioned me again last night.

00:22.310 --> 00:24.800
I can't refuse him a second time.

00:24.800 --> 00:25.830
I see...

00:26.780 --> 00:29.880
So you'll be their healer
 in case of emergencies.

00:29.880 --> 00:32.510
Take it easy for three days and two nights.

00:36.100 --> 00:38.330
Wow, I was so surprised!

00:38.330 --> 00:41.100
I didn't think you'd be joining us, Usato-kun!

00:41.390 --> 00:43.990
And you brought Blurin, too!

00:44.290 --> 00:48.510
You must be trying to help 
Blurin and me get closer!

00:48.510 --> 00:53.450
No, I just didn't have a choice because 
I'm still the only one Blurin likes.

00:53.730 --> 00:57.310
As indifferent as ever, Usato-kun.

00:57.310 --> 00:58.320
Huh?

00:58.800 --> 01:00.070
It's nothing!

01:00.070 --> 01:02.040
Oh, let me introduce you.

01:02.650 --> 01:04.780
They'll be joining us on our expedition.

01:04.780 --> 01:07.280
This is Aruku the knight and Corrin the mage.

01:07.900 --> 01:09.290
It's a pleasure.

01:09.570 --> 01:11.670
I look forward to working with you.

01:11.670 --> 01:14.540
Thanks. It's great to meet you both.

01:14.540 --> 01:18.270
Wait, Aruku... 
Have we met somewhere before?

01:18.270 --> 01:21.100
Yes, I normally work as a castle gatekeeper.

01:21.400 --> 01:22.750
Oh, that's right!

01:22.750 --> 01:24.140
Hero Suzune.

01:24.530 --> 01:25.740
Y-Yes?

01:26.180 --> 01:29.200
The healing magic Usato 
uses isn't omnipotent.

01:29.200 --> 01:33.080
It can cure poison and mend injuries,
but it's all over if you die.

01:34.000 --> 01:36.030
Don't overestimate healing magic.

01:37.310 --> 01:38.560
I understand.

01:38.940 --> 01:44.380
Well, you trained under Siglis. 
I'm sure you'll be fine in most cases.

01:47.500 --> 01:50.410
I've got nothing to say to you.

01:50.410 --> 01:51.380
What?

01:51.380 --> 01:54.640
What? You dying for some advice?

01:54.640 --> 01:56.720
N-No, that's all right.

01:56.720 --> 01:58.670
<i>She'd just hurl abuse at me!</i>

01:59.040 --> 02:00.430
Off you go, then.

02:05.780 --> 02:08.310
Your mentor is really strong.

02:08.310 --> 02:10.580
Huh? What do you mean by that?

02:10.980 --> 02:14.290
Nothing! Come on, time to go!

02:29.540 --> 02:34.210
<i>The Wrong Way to Use Healing Magic</i>

03:45.240 --> 03:48.910
#5 Usato, Back in the Forest!

03:51.550 --> 03:52.820
Sir Kazuki!

03:53.240 --> 03:55.170
What are you doing?!

03:56.360 --> 03:58.580
Well, I'm doing practice swings...

03:58.810 --> 04:01.090
That much is obvious!

04:01.090 --> 04:05.630
I heard you just returned from 
grueling training yesterday.

04:06.310 --> 04:08.440
I can't believe you're back at it so soon.

04:08.780 --> 04:11.770
Well, I got a full night's rest.

04:11.770 --> 04:14.010
I'm fine, Princess Celia.

04:15.490 --> 04:17.000
Are you sure?

04:17.000 --> 04:18.830
You're not overexerting yourself?

04:19.020 --> 04:20.320
Not at all.

04:20.320 --> 04:22.120
See? Look!

04:24.950 --> 04:26.720
V-Very well, then.

04:26.720 --> 04:29.150
Still, please take care of yourself.

04:33.060 --> 04:37.180
Huh... Kazuki came back that exhausted?

04:37.180 --> 04:41.200
Yeah, but he told me he was happy
to get so much combat experience.

04:41.440 --> 04:44.220
He took down lots of monsters on the plains

04:44.220 --> 04:46.380
near a forest called the Darkness of Llinger.

04:46.790 --> 04:49.290
That's where we're going, too.

04:50.200 --> 04:52.220
<i>The Darkness of Llinger...</i>

05:00.620 --> 05:04.140
<i>I wonder if Blurin will feel 
nostalgic going back there.</i>

05:04.780 --> 05:06.550
By the way, Usato-kun...

05:06.550 --> 05:08.580
Is Blurin just going to stay asleep?

05:08.580 --> 05:09.580
Come again?

05:09.580 --> 05:12.320
If he's asleep, well...

05:13.270 --> 05:15.280
Can I pet him?!

05:15.280 --> 05:16.050
Huh?!

05:16.050 --> 05:17.470
It'd be okay right?! Just a little!

05:17.470 --> 05:18.730
Just a tiny bit!

05:22.510 --> 05:24.170
What gives, Usato-kun?!

05:24.420 --> 05:26.910
That's what I should be asking.

05:26.910 --> 05:28.430
What's gotten into you?

05:29.440 --> 05:31.950
That's some attitude after 
slapping a lady's hand!

05:31.950 --> 05:34.190
Have you developed a new fetish?

05:34.190 --> 05:36.110
Uh, I have no idea what you're talking about.

05:39.290 --> 05:41.370
Oh, are you awake, Blurin?

05:43.330 --> 05:46.870
In that case, walk on your own legs, okay?

05:52.510 --> 05:54.540
Hey, now, you okay?

05:54.540 --> 05:55.670
Now's my chance!

05:56.280 --> 05:59.330
Blurin, I'll carry you!

05:59.330 --> 06:00.320
Here! Come on!

06:00.610 --> 06:03.040
Wait, Senpai, that's not...

06:06.170 --> 06:09.220
I-I did it! He's so fluffy!

06:09.220 --> 06:14.700
So this is Blurin's... warmth...

06:14.700 --> 06:16.510
S-Senpai!

06:19.290 --> 06:24.200
Seriously, could you not get yourself 
hurt before we even do any fighting?

06:25.030 --> 06:28.600
Sorry, Usato-kun. I made you 
use your healing magic already.

06:29.070 --> 06:31.230
I mean, I don't really mind that part.

06:32.980 --> 06:35.540
Multiple creatures detected up ahead.

06:35.540 --> 06:37.580
Both of you, please stop there!

06:38.760 --> 06:39.830
Is it monsters?

06:41.980 --> 06:43.430
No, it's...

06:44.280 --> 06:47.060
Tch. Noticed us, did ya?

06:47.910 --> 06:51.390
We were planning to ambush 
you after we surrounded you.

06:55.340 --> 06:58.910
A knight from the royal palace and a mage, eh?

06:58.910 --> 07:01.330
Go ahead, drop all your valuables!

07:01.330 --> 07:01.930
We refuse!

07:02.280 --> 07:04.000
Yeah? You sure?

07:04.000 --> 07:06.670
We got you far outnumbered.

07:07.880 --> 07:10.650
<i>Who the hell are these guys? Bandits?</i>

07:10.650 --> 07:12.520
<i>They aren't scary at all.</i>

07:12.910 --> 07:14.380
U-Usato-kun...

07:14.820 --> 07:17.750
Senpai, don't worry about small fry like them.

07:18.070 --> 07:20.080
Those are real bandits!

07:20.080 --> 07:22.640
I've never seen any before! 
They actually exist!

07:23.080 --> 07:25.410
Senpai, you really are incredible...

07:29.500 --> 07:31.270
Th-This is bad!

07:31.270 --> 07:33.510
They have a blue grizzly with them!

07:36.590 --> 07:38.420
N-No, take a closer look!

07:38.420 --> 07:40.840
It's just a cub!
There's nothing to be afraid of!

07:40.840 --> 07:42.430
H-He's right.

07:42.430 --> 07:44.770
We should catch it and turn it into a pelt.

07:46.010 --> 07:47.450
That's completely—

07:48.020 --> 07:49.440
Completely unforgivable!

07:52.250 --> 07:54.160
Oh, thank goodness. He's still alive.

07:54.790 --> 07:56.910
That was amazing, Senpai!

07:56.910 --> 07:58.490
Great control!

07:59.240 --> 08:02.090
Of course. I practiced a lot, you know.

08:02.430 --> 08:06.550
All right, Senpai! You should go all-out here!

08:06.550 --> 08:09.050
Worst case, I can heal them.

08:09.050 --> 08:10.920
Huh? Go all-out?

08:11.140 --> 08:13.270
She can't use that magic in melee range!

08:13.270 --> 08:15.350
Get her, boys!

08:17.570 --> 08:20.240
Go, Senpai! Mow them down!

08:20.610 --> 08:23.350
Could you not say it like that?

08:25.590 --> 08:29.810
Great job, human stun gun! 
No, human electric eel!

08:29.810 --> 08:32.370
I'm actually going to get mad
if you keep that up.

08:33.110 --> 08:35.140
That shit ain't fair!

08:35.140 --> 08:37.110
If you can see that, surrender!

08:38.010 --> 08:39.280
Another reaction?

08:39.280 --> 08:40.030
Incoming fast.

08:40.280 --> 08:41.040
What?

08:47.590 --> 08:48.620
Boss!

08:48.620 --> 08:52.340
Fall boars?! Their habitat 
should be deeper in the woods!

08:57.040 --> 08:58.670
Blurin, thanks!

09:02.830 --> 09:03.800
Senpai!

09:07.680 --> 09:09.100
U-Usato-kun!

09:09.100 --> 09:11.600
We'll be fine! Hold on tight!

09:27.150 --> 09:29.780
Senpai! Are you all right?! Senpai!

09:29.780 --> 09:31.090
Y-Yeah.

09:31.740 --> 09:33.290
<i>Wait, this place...</i>

09:34.010 --> 09:36.510
<i>It's the same place I was in before.</i>

09:37.050 --> 09:38.260
<i>Which means...</i>

09:38.730 --> 09:41.000
There's a waterfall ahead!

09:41.930 --> 09:44.520
Senpai, take a big breath.

09:44.520 --> 09:45.510
Understood.

09:53.370 --> 09:57.510
...sato-kun! Usato-kun! Hang in there!

10:01.210 --> 10:03.860
I'll carry you somewhere safe.

10:03.860 --> 10:05.790
I'll protect you.

10:06.050 --> 10:09.710
I'm the kind of woman 
who always repays her debts.

10:12.440 --> 10:15.700
Inukami-senpai, I'm fine now.

10:15.700 --> 10:17.600
Also, that's embarrassing.

10:17.600 --> 10:18.190
Huh?!

10:22.860 --> 10:25.600
D-Didn't you wake up a little too fast?!

10:25.890 --> 10:30.030
I was just resting a bit after 
pulling you out of the water...

10:30.410 --> 10:33.130
More importantly, let me heal your wounds.

10:37.570 --> 10:39.230
Th-Thank you.

10:39.230 --> 10:43.130
I'm sorry things turned out
 this way, Usato-kun.

10:43.520 --> 10:47.880
Please don't apologize. 
I'm glad we fell together.

10:49.130 --> 10:50.780
Still...

10:51.220 --> 10:53.720
Never thought I'd end up here again.

10:53.720 --> 10:54.910
Huh?

10:54.910 --> 10:59.420
This is where my captain 
tossed me for my training.

10:59.420 --> 11:02.500
There are tons of monsters
stronger than fall boars here.

11:03.010 --> 11:06.930
<i>The Wrong Way to Use Healing Magic</i>

11:07.590 --> 11:10.360
No food, huh?

11:10.360 --> 11:13.200
I wish we had at least a day's worth...

11:13.640 --> 11:20.370
Usato-kun, shouldn't we leave this forest 
as soon as possible if it's so dangerous?

11:20.820 --> 11:24.270
It's going to be dark soon, 
and the weather doesn't look too good.

11:24.750 --> 11:29.460
We should find a safe place to take shelter 
and then head back tomorrow morning.

11:30.200 --> 11:31.730
That's true.

11:31.730 --> 11:33.670
But where will we find somewhere safe?

11:34.420 --> 11:39.280
I slept in the trees last time. 
Do you think you could do that, Senpai?

11:40.430 --> 11:42.770
I've never climbed a tree before.

11:43.380 --> 11:46.950
I've always wanted to, 
but I was never allowed.

11:47.970 --> 11:52.830
<i>Is Senpai really the sheltered 
daughter of some rich family?</i>

11:53.440 --> 11:55.830
<i>Actually, that's perfectly possible.</i>

11:58.470 --> 12:00.290
In that case, let's rest there.

12:01.290 --> 12:03.570
We'll stay dry even if it rains.

12:03.570 --> 12:06.190
And it's safer than just
wandering into the woods.

12:07.380 --> 12:09.540
Yeah... That's true.

12:09.540 --> 12:14.840
Then, um... why don't you change 
clothes for now, Senpai?

12:14.840 --> 12:17.360
Yeah, I think I will.

12:22.580 --> 12:25.370
Don't peek, okay?

12:26.710 --> 12:29.050
That response is a little hurtful!

12:31.790 --> 12:33.960
Usato-kun, are you ready?

12:33.960 --> 12:37.320
Yup! Let 'er rip anytime!

12:37.320 --> 12:41.850
I still don't really appreciate that 
wording... but here goes!

12:45.610 --> 12:47.060
That's awesome!

12:47.060 --> 12:49.400
Now we have dinner for tonight, Senpai!

12:49.690 --> 12:52.670
Okay, take care of this next, please!

12:53.150 --> 12:54.510
Leave it to me!

12:57.430 --> 12:58.740
Fire!

12:58.740 --> 13:02.330
I'm so glad you're here, Senpai!

13:02.330 --> 13:05.600
I-It's nothing worth crying over.

13:07.270 --> 13:08.930
It's so warm...

13:08.930 --> 13:12.200
Fire is just the best.

13:14.430 --> 13:18.610
Oh... Sorry, Senpai.
I didn't mean to put you out.

13:18.610 --> 13:20.990
N-No, don't mind me.

13:25.830 --> 13:28.150
I think you've gotten even more...

13:28.430 --> 13:30.030
Huh? What did you say?

13:30.030 --> 13:31.460
N-Nothing!

13:42.750 --> 13:44.760
Oh, venom monkeys.

13:44.760 --> 13:46.250
You know what they are?

13:46.890 --> 13:48.350
I've read about them.

13:48.350 --> 13:50.840
It's my first time seeing them in person.

13:53.090 --> 13:54.920
They're coming this way!

13:54.920 --> 14:00.360
They aren't very ferocious, but don't 
touch them. They're poisonous.

14:00.360 --> 14:01.770
Come on. Don't be scared.

14:01.770 --> 14:05.240
Wh-What are you doing?! They're poisonous!

14:05.240 --> 14:12.190
Be that as it may, I've already been 
taken by their intoxicating cuteness.

14:12.610 --> 14:16.160
Come on. Don't be... scared...

14:17.410 --> 14:19.130
What did I tell you?!

14:20.250 --> 14:23.620
They're missing? What do you mean?

14:23.620 --> 14:26.290
Corrin sent word via her familiar.

14:26.600 --> 14:29.400
They encountered an
unexpected herd of monsters

14:29.400 --> 14:32.230
and got separated from Suzune and Usato.

14:34.250 --> 14:37.570
I wasn't sure if I should tell you,

14:37.570 --> 14:42.520
but Celia said I shouldn't 
hide anything from any of you.

14:44.200 --> 14:46.480
Did you send out a search party?

14:46.480 --> 14:50.140
We're gathering one as we speak. 
They'll set out first thing in the morning.

14:49.430 --> 14:51.410
Tomorrow will be too late!

14:51.410 --> 14:52.970
I will go by myself at once.

14:52.970 --> 14:54.240
Sir Kazuki!

14:56.210 --> 14:58.420
Hold on there, Hero Kazuki.

14:58.420 --> 14:59.990
You're...

15:00.360 --> 15:04.830
Hero Suzune and Usato are probably together.

15:05.160 --> 15:06.980
If so, they'll be fine.

15:06.980 --> 15:08.050
Huh?

15:08.360 --> 15:10.440
Usato is my subordinate.

15:10.440 --> 15:11.970
He won't die so easily.

15:12.220 --> 15:16.090
And as long as Usato is fine, 
Hero Suzune will be, too.

15:17.850 --> 15:19.390
Thanks for the meal!

15:19.830 --> 15:24.240
Man, roughing it survival-style is 
a cinch with you around, Senpai!

15:24.590 --> 15:29.270
Do you think of me as just 
some convenient camping tool?

15:29.570 --> 15:35.050
Not at all! I'm just grateful 
from the bottom of my heart.

15:35.050 --> 15:37.730
Well, I'll leave it at that, I guess.

15:40.920 --> 15:44.640
We should take turns sleeping. 
You go first, Senpai.

15:44.640 --> 15:49.310
N-No! You must be tired after 
using so much healing magic!

15:49.310 --> 15:50.630
You first!

15:50.630 --> 15:55.310
You sure? Okay, I'll take you up on that.

16:17.070 --> 16:18.220
Usato-kun...

16:20.340 --> 16:21.890
Are you asleep?

16:23.400 --> 16:25.650
No, not yet.

16:26.170 --> 16:27.760
What is it?

16:31.530 --> 16:36.170
How do you feel about being 
summoned to this world?

16:37.950 --> 16:39.550
How do I feel about it?

16:39.890 --> 16:41.210
Do you want to go home?

16:43.750 --> 16:46.030
That's a difficult question.

16:46.030 --> 16:49.400
I want to go back, 
but at the same time, I don't.

16:50.180 --> 16:52.530
I don't want to go back.

16:55.680 --> 16:58.030
You're not going to ask me why?

16:58.790 --> 17:00.590
Do you want me to?

17:01.330 --> 17:02.710
I do.

17:03.990 --> 17:08.380
I can guess why you don't want to go home.

17:08.790 --> 17:13.810
You like this world a lot better 
than were we came from, right?

17:14.360 --> 17:15.070
Yeah.

17:16.200 --> 17:19.530
I have no lingering attachment
to our old world.

17:20.050 --> 17:21.810
I want to abandon my empty self,

17:21.810 --> 17:26.550
along with my family and my friends,
 and stay here in this world.

17:27.240 --> 17:29.550
I've always dreamed of this...

17:29.550 --> 17:33.790
A chance to free myself from my shackles.

17:35.850 --> 17:38.930
There's nothing holding me back here.

17:39.530 --> 17:43.410
I finally have the freedom
 I've longed for above all else.

17:44.580 --> 17:47.720
I don't think it's wrong to feel that way.

17:47.720 --> 17:48.520
Huh?

17:49.460 --> 17:51.240
What's with that face?

17:52.000 --> 17:55.970
I mean, I wouldn't blame you for being
 completely disillusioned with me.

17:56.220 --> 17:59.100
I always felt the same way.

17:59.760 --> 18:04.530
I wanted to change my mundane 
everyday life, and my mundane self.

18:05.930 --> 18:08.730
So it sounds like we're the same.

18:09.340 --> 18:10.840
Usato-kun...

18:11.640 --> 18:18.340
When we first arrived, all I worried about 
was not getting in your and Kazuki's way.

18:19.750 --> 18:23.370
But now, I'm a part of the Rescue Team,

18:23.370 --> 18:27.510
and I've steeled my resolve to protect you, 
Kazuki, and the people of this kingdom.

18:29.900 --> 18:32.030
What about you, Senpai?

18:34.120 --> 18:39.970
Me, too. I want to protect 
this place as a hero.

18:42.490 --> 18:46.840
Well, then, let's save the people 
of the Llinger Kingdom together.

18:47.180 --> 18:49.780
It has nothing to do with our old world.

18:49.780 --> 18:52.760
We'll protect the place 
we've made for ourselves here.

18:55.000 --> 18:58.100
You've gotten to be so dependable, Usato-kun.

18:58.310 --> 19:01.490
And you've become really human, Senpai.

19:01.900 --> 19:05.500
You were like some untouchable 
flower back home.

19:05.500 --> 19:06.700
Really?

19:06.700 --> 19:10.070
You say that, but you always
 seemed so cold toward me.

19:10.070 --> 19:12.110
What? That's not true...

19:12.110 --> 19:14.070
Well, it's fine.

19:14.070 --> 19:16.050
Rather than being admired,

19:16.320 --> 19:18.630
I much prefer a closer relationship.

19:29.110 --> 19:31.640
I'm going to sleep! Goodnight!

19:32.960 --> 19:35.100
Are you getting shy?

19:40.120 --> 19:44.440
I'm glad we got to talk.
Goodnight, Usato-kun.

19:51.320 --> 19:54.740
This should be the right direction...

19:54.740 --> 19:57.670
Either way, let's watch out for monsters.

19:57.900 --> 20:00.780
Right. I'll be prepared for battle.

20:09.760 --> 20:10.590
Usato-kun!

20:11.430 --> 20:12.270
Yeah.

20:20.460 --> 20:22.100
Blurin!

20:22.780 --> 20:26.130
Hold on a second! You're too 
heavy for a surprise attack...

20:35.360 --> 20:41.390
D-Dame Suzune... Sir Usato...

20:42.880 --> 20:45.010
Aruku!

20:45.370 --> 20:51.000
The bear cub suddenly ran off while 
we were searching in the forest.

20:51.670 --> 20:54.880
I thought maybe he'd picked up
 your scent and gave chase.

20:54.880 --> 20:57.120
Y-You did a good job.

20:57.730 --> 21:01.530
Blurin must have caught 
your scent, Usato-kun.

21:01.880 --> 21:03.230
Very impressive, Blurin!

21:10.030 --> 21:11.090
Blurin?

21:15.120 --> 21:17.490
Usato-kun, what is this place?

21:17.490 --> 21:20.590
This is the den where Blurin used to live.

21:21.410 --> 21:24.250
His parents were killed
by a giant snake monster.

21:25.170 --> 21:26.520
I see...

21:28.630 --> 21:29.660
Blurin...

21:37.250 --> 21:39.750
Hey, Usato-kun, is this...

21:39.750 --> 21:42.810
I think he's urging us to leave.

21:44.600 --> 21:47.070
It looks like Blurin has decided

21:47.490 --> 21:50.410
that his place is by your side, Usato-kun.

21:55.150 --> 21:56.070
Well...

21:58.220 --> 22:00.680
Let's head back, Usato-kun.

22:03.420 --> 22:05.330
Yeah, let's go back...

22:05.910 --> 22:07.610
to where we belong!
